          <change when="2024-01-14T06:27:08-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Finalized - done</change>
          <change when="2024-01-14T06:27:02-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Commit - I've retained (Ἀρσ(ινόῃ) in lin2 (I was too agnostic back then). I tacitly fixed ὁμολογοῦμεν in lin7; ὁμολογο(ῦ)μεν was the old way of representing superscript υ (ditto ἀμφόδου in lin4, from I where I removed the BL entry). I also hanged the accent of the name in lin11.</change>
          <change when="2024-01-12T17:37:07-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - AcceptText - OK. To adjust at finalization.</change>
          <change when="2024-01-12T15:42:15-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/FabianDr.Reiter">Vote - AcceptText - Ok, but, please adjust app. to l. 1: BL I 436 puts the accent correctly in Φλαουίων (not Φλαούιων); one might add „λαμπρρS papyrus“.&#xD;
In app. to l. 2 „ϊνS papyrus“ has to be added.&#xD;
L. 7 πόλε]ω̣ς: The diagonal stroke of ε is in fact clearly visible on the photo, so the word should rather be transcribed πόλ]εως.&#xD;
   ὁμολογο(ῦ)μεν &gt; ὁμολογοῦμεν (N. Gonis, ZPE 159, 2007, 269)</change>
